  "_link_comment": "Inter-node: 16 Gbps / 0.3 ms measured on the 10.212 fabric. Intra-node: same-host P/D handoff, measured ~0-2 ms for a 512-token prefix, modelled as 50 GB/s over PCIe with 1 us per-layer latency. Declaring the intra-node link switches the topology to [tp, slots_per_node, num_nodes] so the network model can tell a same-domain handoff from a cross-domain one.",
  "_handoff_comment": "KV-heavy variant: 1250-token prompts carry 184 MB of KV per request, and the measured producer ceiling (115-314 MB/s, 585-731 ms per handoff) is what limits the real fabric -- a single Prefill sustains ~1.4 req/s of such handoffs, not the wire's 2 GB/s. Set kv_egress_gbps = 0.26 to charge that path; measured consequence on 2026-09-15: a 200-request 14 req/s CNN replay no longer keeps up (7.4 req/s) whereas the wire value does (13.5 req/s) -- pick the value that matches the workload's regime.",
